{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert Markdown files from the terminal and preview the text generators.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingTheCommandLineTools"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Using the Command-Line Tools"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The MarkdownKit package contains two command-line tools. Both are provided to serve as a demo and as a basis for customization to specific use cases, and both are only functional on macOS. The simplest way to build and run them is the Swift Package Manager (SPM), in a checkout of the repository.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Convert-Markdown-files","level":3,"text":"Convert Markdown files","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MarkdownKitProcess","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownKitProcess/MarkdownKitProcess.swift","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that outputs Markdown content (parsed with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") either as HTML, RTF, RTFD, or pretty-printed text, including the option to output ANSI-compliant markup. The tool either outputs a single Markdown text file into an output file or, when applied to a folder, outputs all Markdown files within the folder into output files in a target folder. Existing output files are not touched unless the option ","type":"text"},{"code":"--overwrite","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is used.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["> git clone https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit.git","> cd swift-markdownkit","> swift run MarkdownKitProcess --help","USAGE: MarkdownKitProcess [<option> ...] <source> [<target>]","OPTIONS:","  -f, --format <format>","      Output format: 'text' (plain text, default), 'ansi' (text marked up with ANSI escape codes), 'html', 'rtf', or 'rtfd'.","  -w, --width <columns>","      Width in columns of the formats 'text' and 'ansi', at least 10 (default: the width of the terminal, or 80).","  -o, --overwrite","      Replaces output files which already exist. Without this option, they are not touched.","  -h, --help","      Prints this usage description.","PARAMETERS:","  <source>","      A Markdown file, or a directory of Markdown files (the files ending in '.md').","  <target>","      The file, or the directory into which the converted files are written. The converted","      file of 'a.md' is called 'a.txt' ('text' and 'ansi'), 'a.html', 'a.rtf' or 'a.rtfd'.","      '-' prints the output (not possible for 'rtfd'). If there is no target, the converted","      files are written next to the source files.","Diagrams in fenced code blocks with language 'mermaid' are drawn in the format 'rtfd'.","RTF files cannot contain images: the format 'rtf' shows the code of a diagram."],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Include-diagrams","level":3,"text":"Include diagrams","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The format ","type":"text"},{"code":"rtfd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" includes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://mermaid.js.org","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" diagrams as images (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). RTF files cannot contain the images that ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" creates, so the format ","type":"text"},{"code":"rtf","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shows the code of a diagram instead. The directory ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Examples/Demo.md","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" contains a Markdown file with the demo document of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MarkdownViewer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sample app, including two diagrams, for trying the tool:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["> swift run MarkdownKitProcess --format rtfd Examples/Demo.md /tmp/Demo.rtfd","converted 'Demo.md' into 'Demo.rtfd'","> swift run MarkdownKitProcess --format rtfd Examples/Demo.md /tmp/Demo.rtfd","error: '/tmp/Demo.rtfd' already exists (use --overwrite to replace it)","> swift run MarkdownKitProcess --format rtfd --overwrite Examples/Demo.md /tmp/Demo.rtfd","converted 'Demo.md' into 'Demo.rtfd'"],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Preview-the-text-generators","level":3,"text":"Preview the text generators","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A second tool, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownTermViewer/main.swift","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", does not read any files. It prints a demo document with the features of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (the document displayed by the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MarkdownViewer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sample app: formatted text, tables, task lists, code blocks, …) either as plain text (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/StringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") or marked up with ANSI escape codes (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TerminalGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). This is a quick way to see what the text generators produce:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["> swift run MarkdownTermViewer --help","USAGE: MarkdownTermViewer [<option> ...]","OPTIONS:","  -f, --format <format>","      Output format: 'text' (plain text, default) or 'ansi' (marked up with ANSI escape codes).","  -w, --width <columns>","      Width in columns, at least 10 (default: the width of the terminal, or 80).","  -h, --help","      Prints this usage description.","> swift run MarkdownTermViewer --format ansi --width 60"],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The output of ","type":"text"},{"code":"--format ansi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is only rendered correctly by a terminal. Xcode’s console shows the escape sequences as raw characters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams":{"abstract":[{"text":"Show fenced code blocks with the language ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as diagrams in attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Drawing Mermaid Diagrams","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/drawingmermaiddiagrams"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser":{"abstract":[{"code":"FullMarkdownParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects are used to parse Markdown text represented as a string using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all features of MarkdownKit: the syntax of the CommonMark specification and all extensions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that MarkdownKit implements.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FullMarkdownParser"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FullMarkdownParser"}],"role":"symbol","title":"FullMarkdownParser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/fullmarkdownparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert a parsed Markdown document into HTML, attributed strings, plain text or text for ANSI terminals.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Generating Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/generatingoutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingTerminalOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Format Markdown documents as plain text, or as text with ANSI styling for terminals.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingTerminalOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Generating Plain Text and Terminal Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/generatingterminaloutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/RenderingUntrustedMarkdown":{"abstract":[{"text":"Restrict what raw HTML, links and images in a document may do when the Markdown does not come from you.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/RenderingUntrustedMarkdown","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Rendering Untrusted Markdown","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/renderinguntrustedmarkdown"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/StringGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"StringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into formatted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plain text strings with word wrapping and indentation support. The implementation is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extensible allowing subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"StringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to override how individual Markdown","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"structures are converted into strings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StringGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/StringGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StringGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"StringGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/stringgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TerminalGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"TerminalGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into text for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ANSI-compliant terminals, with word wrapping, indentation, and styled text. The result is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"marked up with ANSI escape sequences. The implementation is extensible allowing subclasses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"TerminalGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to override how individual Markdown structures are converted into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"styled text.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TerminalGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TerminalGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TerminalGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"TerminalGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/terminalgenerator"},"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Examples/Demo.md":{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Examples/Demo.md","title":"Examples","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"Examples","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Examples/Demo.md"},"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownKitProcess/MarkdownKitProcess.swift":{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownKitProcess/MarkdownKitProcess.swift","title":"very simple command-line tool","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"very simple command-line tool","type":"text"}],"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownKitProcess/MarkdownKitProcess.swift"},"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownTermViewer/main.swift":{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownTermViewer/main.swift","title":"MarkdownTermViewer","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"MarkdownTermViewer","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownTermViewer/main.swift"},"https://mermaid.js.org":{"identifier":"https://mermaid.js.org","title":"Mermaid","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Mermaid","type":"text"}],"type":"link","url":"https://mermaid.js.org"}},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingTerminalOutput"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"anchor":"Generating-output","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/RenderingUntrustedMarkdown"],"title":"Generating output"}],"variants":[{"paths":["/documentation/markdownkit/usingthecommandlinetools"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}]}